  "documentation": {
    "content": "# Runbook: GKE Pod CrashLoopBackOff\n**Severity:** CRITICAL\n**Metric:** logging.googleapis.com/user/CrashLoopBackOff\n\n## 1. Overview\nThis alert triggers when a container in the netapp-prod-monitoring project frequently restarts.\n\n## 2. Immediate Diagnostic Steps\n1. Identify the Crashing Pod: kubectl get pods -A | grep -i <container_name>\n2. Inspect Status & Events: kubectl describe pod <pod_name> -n <namespace>\n3. Check Previous Logs: kubectl logs <pod_name> -n <namespace> -c <container_name> --previous\n\n## 3. Common Root Causes\n- Application Crash (Exit Code 1)\n- OOMKilled (Increase Memory limits)\n- Liveness Probe Failure\n- Permission Denied (Verify IAM)\n- Config/Secret Missing",
